I have had 7 characters take the amulet from the Sanctum.
Of these, 6 have made it to the Astral plane.
Of these, 4 have ascended.
Of these, 2 Valkyries and 2 Priestesses.
Of all these, only a single has tried any kind of conduct.

This priestess survived.

She started with +oIdentify and +oCure Blindness. I don't remember an
awful lot about the early part of the game, except there were massive
amounts of bones-files down the mines and around the oracle. Sokoban
provided reflection, the ghosts gave me +oRemove Curse (noncursed from
the start - how perfect can you get??!), (BoH, an uncursed luckstone,
and +oForce Bolt and various other minor goodies, such as jumping boots.

A werewolf in minetown tried to summon companions, so I charmed him and 
his wolf friend. Trusty was a large dog by then, and I decided to check 
out further in the mines with 3 d's. A housecat died and dropped a magic 
whistle, Trusty polyed into a Vampire Bat, but I let him eat a chameleon 
which turned him into a stone golem. Mine's end was the winecellar, 
which provided me with more holy-water material. I didn't bother with 
the jewellery - why sell stones to shopkeepers when Trusty will kill 
them for you? Found speed boots in a shop, and gauntlets of dexterity 
either in a shop or lying around.

Then we went to look for an altar. Minetown was coaligned and the 
bones+sokoban was enough money for protection. The next altar was a 
coaligned temple on level 21. And beside the Quest-altars, that was it! 

Pets got killed sooner or later - Oz the werewolf lasted a fair while, 
but Trusty died from a shop mimic. Don't know where the wolf went. I 
charmed those my /, ? or +oCreate Monster generated peaceful and led 
them up the stairs from my temple - pets and peacefuls don't work well 
with Stormbringer... A pet finally killed the priest though, which was 
actually a boon; now the sacrifices-to-be no longer fled from the altar!

I found Excalibur in a bonesfile, and got Orcrist from sacrificing. I 
wacked it abit, then went on the Quest with a +4 red dragon scales and 
my +5 mace. Next sacrifial gift was Ogresmasher - and at this point I 
gave up on getting something useful out of Anshur. I went on to pray for 
spellbooks instead. He wasn't very generous there either, but it got me 
crowned and provided Stormbringer at least. Polypiling got me more 
interesting books, including +MMapping. A gray dragon exhausted 2 
wands of turn undead and 3 scrolls of charging before dropping scales. 
At this point the thought of conducts started creeping into my head, 
since I had most of the AK already. When I dropped a MMF at 5 squares 
with arrows and no damage to myself, the thought got stronger.

There is a very particular feeling you get when you ID the castle-/oW - 
and then *put it back in the chest*.

I had 4 magic markers all together (none polypiled), but used almost a 
whole one on guess-writing ?oCharging TWICE. Damned (M)MF's. Glad I had 
+Identify and +Magic Mapping. Major convenience, no external notes 
needed.

TIP: If you don't want to wish, and you're not genociding mind flayers; 
keep an extra scroll of each kind you might need, so you can re-ID them 
later. Guess-writing for non-wizards is a pain.

Paid those Demons I could, whacked the others. Fireballed the minor 
lich types, magic missile and Stormbringer for the others. After the two 
mindwipes, (M)MF's were elevated to /oDeath status. No regrets. I 
couldn't afford to lose more memories.

I had a 2 or 3 purple worms at various points, but they kept turning 
into baby dragons the moment I turned my back on them!

An electric eel almost made me break wishing conduct; it vapourized my
=s of Conflict, Free Action, teleControl (no teleportitis at that
point: I used it with cursed ?oTeleport to get to stash level) and one
Levitation. I polypiled surplus rings until I got them back; =Free
Action was the last to show up on the last ring standing, on the last
/oPolymorph charge. *phew!*

In the sanctum someone summoned a cockatrice. Not even the high priest 
of Moloch was immune to that little birdie, so getting the amulet was 
actually extremely fast.

Used my ?oTeleports to quickly get from staircase to staircase (though 
the mysterious force obviously really loved level 40. I saw it enough 
times..). A last prayer at level 21, then up we went.

Earth no problem, Fire no problem (ran away from the Archon), Rodney 
turned up on Air which was NOT NICE. I /oTeleported away the air 
elementals and cozied up to the steam vortices so they would give me 
sanctuary. Confused gold detection found the portals, wand of death 
found Rodney... Water was a breeze - I used conflict on all planes 
anyway.

Forgot to take it off for Astral. :( This problem was quickly alleviated 
when someone summoned a cockatrice. Like in the sanctum, this made the 
process immensely faster. I arrived to the left near Pestilence, but the 
altar was neutral so not even my helm of OA would help. Next was death. 
Suprisingly enough he went down to the rubber chicken, and the altar was 
chaotic.

